+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-and-sequential-booking-ids.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-and-sequential-booking-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use half-open UTC day intervals and sequential booking IDs"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Rental dates must represent complete UTC days, and booking identifiers must be usable by later
+operations such as cancellation without relying on time or randomness.
+
+## Decision
+
+Represent rental periods as half-open UTC intervals `[start, end)`. Require both endpoints to be
+midnight UTC and require `end` to be after `start`. Generate booking IDs with an instance-local,
+monotonically increasing counter.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Two rentals may touch at an endpoint without conflicting. Booking IDs are deterministic within a
+service instance and unique for its lifetime.
